[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186179730 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a8478761-1f4e-5c9d-a634-3425df7889e5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179592 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k+1)!$ for any $k \\geq 2?$\n\nI. $(k+1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k-1)$\n\nII. $(k+1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k-1)!$\n\nIII. $(k+1) \\cdot k$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179659 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-14a5adf6-2b28-57e0-9971-452cd7b77a19" "question-c9507815-c165-5ef4-b7fc-1303dcd3fdc4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179660 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8948ecd0-03b4-5bf8-9bc2-1467d2b61321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8478761-1f4e-5c9d-a634-3425df7889e5" :question/id #uuid "a8478761-1f4e-5c9d-a634-3425df7889e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124490" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k-1)!$ for any $k\\ge 4?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have \n\n$$\n(k-1)!=(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)\\cdot (k-4)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k-1)! & =(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot \\overset{(k-3)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(k-3)\\cdot (k-4)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)!\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc7e4408-fbc9-5f18-bf91-1f672892b184"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc7e4408-fbc9-5f18-bf91-1f672892b184" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7e4408-fbc9-5f18-bf91-1f672892b184" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0444fa0-516b-5c9b-82d3-af49b3feedc9" "answer-8408d7f7-986c-53a7-8060-d0e712a043fb" "answer-7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" "answer-ea8b46c1-8a21-5eb2-9692-195052a1df74" "answer-ac845e78-dfdf-51a2-9552-e2548a59f300"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0444fa0-516b-5c9b-82d3-af49b3feedc9" :answer/id #uuid "f0444fa0-516b-5c9b-82d3-af49b3feedc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8408d7f7-986c-53a7-8060-d0e712a043fb" :answer/id #uuid "8408d7f7-986c-53a7-8060-d0e712a043fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" :answer/id #uuid "7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)!" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea8b46c1-8a21-5eb2-9692-195052a1df74" :answer/id #uuid "ea8b46c1-8a21-5eb2-9692-195052a1df74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac845e78-dfdf-51a2-9552-e2548a59f300" :answer/id #uuid "ac845e78-dfdf-51a2-9552-e2548a59f300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-3)!" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-14a5adf6-2b28-57e0-9971-452cd7b77a19" :question/id #uuid "14a5adf6-2b28-57e0-9971-452cd7b77a19" :question/math-academy-id "q-122060" :question/problem "Given that $n\\ge 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n! & =n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)! \\\\ (n+1)! & =(n+1)\\cdot n!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ and $n!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^{2}} & =\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{n!\\cdot n!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n-2)!\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!}{n!\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-2)!}\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bebaea8-1ea1-5395-8e7f-1a00a59795e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bebaea8-1ea1-5395-8e7f-1a00a59795e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bebaea8-1ea1-5395-8e7f-1a00a59795e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46ff1943-a30d-5d55-b989-75cc58c7e295" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b209c69e-bcd5-5443-a258-9983e0b3b3ad" "answer-1b2bd303-a67e-5430-8fae-4d34f010ab2f" "answer-723c2e65-97d9-5e30-8f62-7d0b9ac25429" "answer-46ff1943-a30d-5d55-b989-75cc58c7e295" "answer-90c4d29d-6f34-5c61-80e8-b426e05a3941"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b209c69e-bcd5-5443-a258-9983e0b3b3ad" :answer/id #uuid "b209c69e-bcd5-5443-a258-9983e0b3b3ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b2bd303-a67e-5430-8fae-4d34f010ab2f" :answer/id #uuid "1b2bd303-a67e-5430-8fae-4d34f010ab2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-723c2e65-97d9-5e30-8f62-7d0b9ac25429" :answer/id #uuid "723c2e65-97d9-5e30-8f62-7d0b9ac25429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n(n+1)}{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ff1943-a30d-5d55-b989-75cc58c7e295" :answer/id #uuid "46ff1943-a30d-5d55-b989-75cc58c7e295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c4d29d-6f34-5c61-80e8-b426e05a3941" :answer/id #uuid "90c4d29d-6f34-5c61-80e8-b426e05a3941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}-1}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9507815-c165-5ef4-b7fc-1303dcd3fdc4" :question/id #uuid "c9507815-c165-5ef4-b7fc-1303dcd3fdc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122049" :question/problem "Given that $n\\ge 0$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n+3)!}{n!}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(n+3)!=(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $n!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n+3)!}{n!} & =\\frac{(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!}{n!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}} \\\\  & =(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-96838955-c6ff-5947-a190-f1ef251ea9e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-96838955-c6ff-5947-a190-f1ef251ea9e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "96838955-c6ff-5947-a190-f1ef251ea9e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6e71356-751a-5b88-bb29-4ab075926417" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5263ce43-a391-52ed-a678-006a7cae38af" "answer-c6e71356-751a-5b88-bb29-4ab075926417" "answer-e76e9a1a-cb09-51eb-bef3-1b4f0aeb11c7" "answer-ed427fb4-d7c8-5799-866d-63deafd02049" "answer-c58cfce8-e369-5afc-b6e2-87bc6a2d0b7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5263ce43-a391-52ed-a678-006a7cae38af" :answer/id #uuid "5263ce43-a391-52ed-a678-006a7cae38af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6e71356-751a-5b88-bb29-4ab075926417" :answer/id #uuid "c6e71356-751a-5b88-bb29-4ab075926417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e76e9a1a-cb09-51eb-bef3-1b4f0aeb11c7" :answer/id #uuid "e76e9a1a-cb09-51eb-bef3-1b4f0aeb11c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n+2)(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed427fb4-d7c8-5799-866d-63deafd02049" :answer/id #uuid "ed427fb4-d7c8-5799-866d-63deafd02049" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c58cfce8-e369-5afc-b6e2-87bc6a2d0b7d" :answer/id #uuid "c58cfce8-e369-5afc-b6e2-87bc6a2d0b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n(n+2)(n+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8948ecd0-03b4-5bf8-9bc2-1467d2b61321" :question/id #uuid "8948ecd0-03b4-5bf8-9bc2-1467d2b61321" :question/math-academy-id "q-79305" :question/problem "Given that $m\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\text{ }(m-1)!}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n(m+2)!=(m+2)(m+1)(m)(m-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(m+2)$ and $(m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\text{ }(m-1)!} & =\\frac{(m+2)\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m\\cdot (m-1)!}{(m+2)\\cdot (m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(m+2)}\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}}{\\cancel{(m+2)}\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}} \\\\  & =(m+1)\\cdot m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}+m\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3466d9a9-8d93-5dce-a113-2a97b5048512"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3466d9a9-8d93-5dce-a113-2a97b5048512" :answer-field/id #uuid "3466d9a9-8d93-5dce-a113-2a97b5048512" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5fef2f0c-7256-578e-b6f0-95a297ff2ae3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1584deb7-4764-5143-864e-22d0f7584563" "answer-ea990394-d45f-5925-aedd-845ccc8ee565" "answer-59ec1f07-6b74-59a0-bd26-0c900add0f71" "answer-5fef2f0c-7256-578e-b6f0-95a297ff2ae3" "answer-6b2ad49e-66ce-572e-83ee-22eb483326c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1584deb7-4764-5143-864e-22d0f7584563" :answer/id #uuid "1584deb7-4764-5143-864e-22d0f7584563" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{m+1}{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea990394-d45f-5925-aedd-845ccc8ee565" :answer/id #uuid "ea990394-d45f-5925-aedd-845ccc8ee565" :answer/